+# Agent Note: Daily token usage statistics panel
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-15-daily-token-usage-panel.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+The harness records provider-reported token usage in every session log (`assistant/message.usage` and streaming `assistant/chunk` usage samples), and token-meter projects it per session, but nothing answers the everyday question "how many tokens did I use yesterday / this week / across models?" Cross-session, per-day aggregation — and a GUI to ask it with — did not exist.
+
+## Decision
+
+Two new packages plus one API method:
+
+- **`@deepseek-ai/dsh-usage-query`** (host) provides the `ctx.usageQuery` service. `query(request)` reads the logical corpus through `ctx.sessionQuery` (`listSessions` + `readSession`), folds usage samples with a last-wins `(turn, step)` rule (a final `assistant/message` usage replaces the same step's earlier `assistant/chunk` sample, mirroring token-meter's `tokenUsage` projection), attributes each sample to the newest preceding `request/header`'s `provider/model` (else the `unknown` label) and to the sample event's **local calendar day**, then groups by any non-empty, duplicate-free subset of `day` / `model` / `session`. The response is deterministic rows plus a grand total; validation failures and a missing `sessionQuery` fail loudly before any corpus read. The service is read-only: no agent, prompt, or provider interaction.
+- **`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-usage`** (web client) registers a `sidebar.footer.action` trigger (icon-only on the collapsed rail) that opens a modal: date presets (today / last 7 / last 30 / all, or two custom date inputs), group-by chips over the three dimensions (the last dimension cannot be switched off), a bar strip for the first grouped dimension, and a grouped totals table with a grand-total footer. Every control change issues one `usage.query` call; the plugin holds no state beyond the trigger's open flag.
+- **`usage.query`** joins `RpcMethodMap` as a new apiproxy domain (`api/usage.ts` + `api/usage.schema.ts` + fetch routes + `IApiClient.usage`), delegating to `ctx.usageQuery` and reporting the service's absence as an `internal` error. The wire view types are defined in the browser-safe `api/` layer and re-exported through connection / api-remotes for client consumption.
+
+The web bundle mounts both packages (`usage-query` host row, `ui-usage` browser row); the base/TUI composition is untouched.
+
+## Testing
+
+Host folds and service behavior are pinned by 27 unit tests with 100% per-file coverage (`packages/usage/usage-query`), including the last-wins replacement rule, header attribution, window filtering, every dimension combination, sorting, and the loud failure paths. The client panel is pinned by 21 jsdom tests (100% coverage on `src/client`) covering presets, custom dates, group toggles, the last-dimension guard, bars, table cells, unknown-model labels, error/empty/loading states, and close paths; the plugin bench verifies registration and HMR-safe teardown. The apiproxy suite (374 tests) and the web-app bundle composition tests pass unchanged.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Extend token-meter's projection to a daily ledger** — rejected. `tokenUsage` is a per-session projection over the projection seam; a cross-session, parameterized aggregation is a different shape (window + grouping), and entangling it with the meter's compaction-facing service would couple a read-only analytics surface to pressure accounting.
+
+**A durable per-day ledger written by a live listener** — rejected for the first cut. It would need backfill, crash reconciliation, and storage ownership for a benefit (faster repeated queries) the corpus scan already covers at personal scale; the scan is stateless and always consistent with the logs.
+
+**A Typert Remote instead of an apiproxy method** — rejected. The panel is a request/response query over a new domain; the apiproxy method table is the established, schema-validated channel for exactly that (settings, models, jobs), and it keeps the client call `api.usage.query(...)` typed end to end without a generated Remote.
+
+**Grouping as a single dimension picker** — rejected per request: the panel deliberately supports any combination of dimensions (day × model × session) so "per model per day" and similar pivot views work without new endpoints.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Users get a local, offline view of their token consumption per day, model, and session from data the harness already logs — no provider API, no new storage format, no model-visible surface change. The cost: every query replays the session corpus (fine at personal scale; a durable ledger remains the documented follow-up), and counts are whole-log-scoped (compacted-away steps still count, matching `tokenUsage` semantics). The `unknown` model label makes pre-header samples visible rather than dropped.
