+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-usage
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+Token usage statistics panel for the Web GUI: a sidebar-foot trigger (icon-only on the collapsed rail) that opens a modal over the `usage.query` API. The panel combines date presets (today / last 7 days / last 30 days / all time, or two custom date inputs) with free-form grouping — any non-empty combination of **day / model / session** — and renders a bar strip for the first grouped dimension plus a grouped totals table (input, output, cache read, cache write, total, requests) with a grand-total footer.
+
+The panel is a **snapshot**: it captures the open moment as the `asOf` cutoff and sends it with every query, so usage produced after the panel opened stays out of the view (the summary shows the cutoff time); closing and reopening the panel refreshes the moment.
+
+## Data flow
+
+Every control change issues one unary `usage.query` call carrying the frozen `asOf` cutoff; the plugin holds no state beyond the trigger's component-local open flag. Rows carry exactly the requested dimensions, so the table headers and the bar labels follow the selection. Unknown-model samples render a localized `unknown model` label. Transport-level failures (abort, timeout, connection loss) surface as the error note instead of an endless spinner.
+
+## Composition
+
+```yaml
+- id: ui-usage
+  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-usage'
+```
+
+The node half is inert (the plugin appears in the Loader tree); the browser half registers the `sidebar.footer.action` entry and the `usage` locale namespace. Requires the connection (for the API face), slots, and locale services, all present in the web bundle.
+
+## Model Experience
+
+None, as the panel only calls the trusted read-only usage domain and renders its answer; it never sends a prompt, message, schema, tool, or model request.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+None.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- **Data is as fresh as the last query** — the panel does not subscribe to session events; a long-open panel shows the corpus as of its last control change.
+- **Bars normalize to the largest row** — a single outlier row makes smaller rows visually tiny; a log-scale toggle is deferred.
